 ],
 "title": "Oleaginous Yeast Metabolic Engineering and Lipid Production",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around oleaginous yeasts, specifically Rhodosporidium toruloides and Rhodotorula toruloides, which are capable of lipid accumulation and production. These organisms can utilize crude glycerol as a growth factor and produce carotenoids and lipids. Rhodotorula glutinis is another oleaginous yeast that can grow on crude glycerol and produce torulene. The cluster also includes various chemical compounds such as carotenoids, lipids, and nitrogen, which are involved in the metabolic processes of these organisms. Metabolic engineering is a key process in this cluster, enabling the production of lipids and other compounds in oleaginous yeasts.",
